            <ArticleTitle>Pericardial fat flap: surgical technique for infection control after graft replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1510/mmcts.2017.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical treatment of mycotic aneurysm of the thoracic aorta is challenging because contamination from surrounding tissues may occur even after complete debridement with a prosthetic graft replacement of the aneurysm. This study describes the simple but very useful technique of using a pericardial fat flap to protect the prosthetic graft from reinfection.</AbstractText>
